                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/cpld.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This needs to go in a separate commit where you're adding support for firmware update of this CPLD.  We shouldn't be modifying schemas as a fundamental part of adding a system.\n\nYou're going to have to add support in phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt at the same time."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/cpld.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "andychung113",
                        "username": "andychung113"
                    },
                    "message": "Removed from this patch. We already created separate commit.\nEntity manager schema:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/85255\nphosphor-bmc-code-mgmt change:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/85223"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/exposes_record.json",
                    "line": 181,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: PCIeSwitchFirmware?  Use PCIe capitalization rather than something different.  I'm guessing \"SW\" means \"switch\" and not \"software\" so be clear.  Characters are cheap; clarity is not."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/exposes_record.json",
                    "line": 181,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "andychung113",
                        "username": "andychung113"
                    },
                    "message": "Will modify the naming and create separate commit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 907,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "These all appear to be VRMs that are not currently supported by dbus-sensors either and probably not even with support in the kernel.  You can't put the entity-manager config in before the rest of the software support."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 907,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "andychung113",
                        "username": "andychung113"
                    },
                    "message": "Remove not supported device from patch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/pcie_switch.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This should be handled in a separate commit where you add support for updating PCIe switch firmware."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/pcie_switch.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "andychung113",
                        "username": "andychung113"
                    },
                    "message": "Will create separate commit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/pcie_switch.json",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: PCIe."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/pcie_switch.json",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "andychung113",
                        "username": "andychung113"
                    },
                    "message": "Will create separate commit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/pcie_switch.json",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How is the firmware updated on this device?  I believe there is already support for SPI-NOR based update without specifying it as a \"PCIe switch\" specifically."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/pcie_switch.json",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "DirkChen0105",
                        "email": "dirkchen@amd.com",
                        "username": "DirkChen0105"
                    },
                    "message": "The SPI flash is connected behind the FT4222, which is a USB-to-SPI bridge IC.\nTherefore, the BMC communicates with the FT4222 using the vendor\u2019s libraries (libft4222 and libftd2xx) to write to the SPI flash.\n\nBMC \u2192 USB hub \u2192 USB hub \u2192 FT4222 \u2192 SPI flash"
                }
            ],
