            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "DirkChen0105",
                        "email": "dirkchen@amd.com",
                        "username": "DirkChen0105"
                    },
                    "message": "The SPI flash is connected behind the FT4222, which is a USB-to-SPI bridge IC.\nTherefore, the BMC communicates with the FT4222 using the vendor\u2019s libraries (libft4222 and libftd2xx) to write to the SPI flash.\n\nBMC \u2192 USB hub \u2192 USB hub \u2192 FT4222 \u2192 SPI flash"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> Therefore, the BMC communicates with the FT4222 using the vendor\u2019s libraries (libft4222 and libftd2xx) to write to the SPI flash.\n\nNope, this is unacceptable to pick up vendor libraries.  If it isn't open source and publicly available it cannot be implemented in openbmc.\n\nWe need to either make an open source implementation or pick another hardware solution here."
                }
            ],
